{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Profiling Hardware Accelerated Computations on Google Colab\n",
    "\n",
    "[![Open In Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)](https://colab.research.google.com/github/erolrecep/profiling_hardware_accelerated_computations/blob/main/notebooks/cuda_profiling_colab_workshop.ipynb)\n",
    "\n",
    "This interactive notebook allows you to test, run, and profile native CUDA C and PyTorch GPU kernels on a **free cloud NVIDIA GPU** (Tesla T4 / A100 / L4).\n",
    "\n",
    "You will generate live **NVIDIA Nsight Systems (`.nsys-rep`)**, **NVIDIA Nsight Compute (`.ncu-rep`)**, and **PyTorch Kineto (`.json`)** traces, and compare your live terminal outputs with the visual reference snapshots in the repository!\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Prerequisite**: In Google Colab, make sure you are using a GPU runtime:  \n",
    "> `Runtime` -> `Change runtime type` -> Select **T4 GPU** or **A100 GPU**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Verify Cloud GPU & Profiler Tooling"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!nvidia-smi\n",
    "!nvcc --version\n",
    "!nsys --version\n",
    "!ncu --version"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Clone Repository & Setup Environment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Clone the repository and navigate inside\n",
    "!rm -rf profiling_hardware_accelerated_computations\n",
    "!git clone https://github.com/erolrecep/profiling_hardware_accelerated_computations.git\n",
    "%cd profiling_hardware_accelerated_computations\n",
    "\n",
    "# Install dependencies\n",
    "!pip install -q numba pytest scalene memray matplotlib tabulate rich"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Automated Parity Verification Suite\n",
    "Run tests across all 6 backends to verify numerical parity against double-precision NumPy references ($\epsilon \\le 10^{-4}$)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pytest tests/ -v"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Compile Native CUDA C Kernels\n",
    "Compiles naive, 2D shared memory tiled ($B=16$), vectorized `float4`, and cuBLAS GEMM kernels, along with the Mandelbrot CUDA C suite."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Detect architecture (sm_75 for T4, sm_80 for A100)\n",
    "!nvcc -O3 -arch=native -lcublas src/gemm/gemm_cuda.cu -o src/gemm/gemm_cuda\n",
    "!nvcc -O3 -arch=native src/mandelbrot/mandelbrot_cuda.cu -o src/mandelbrot/mandelbrot_cuda\n",
    "!ls -lh src/gemm/gemm_cuda src/mandelbrot/mandelbrot_cuda"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. NVIDIA Nsight Systems (`nsys`): Macro Timeline Trace\n",
    "Capture host and GPU timeline events with `--stats=true` to view the **CUDA API Summary**, **Kernel Summary**, and **Memory Transfer Summary** directly in your terminal!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!mkdir -p telemetry\n",
    "!nsys profile \\\n",
    "    --trace=cuda,nvtx,osrt \\\n",
    "    --stats=true \\\n",
    "    --force-overwrite=true \\\n",
    "    --output=telemetry/colab_nsys_gemm \\\n",
    "    ./src/gemm/gemm_cuda 1024 10"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Compare with Reference Snapshot\n",
    "Notice how `cudaStreamSynchronize` dominates host time and how the shared memory tiled kernel reduces GPU time by over 2.5x!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from IPython.display import Image, display\n",
    "display(Image(\"presentation/images/snapshots/snapshot_nsys_timeline.png\", width=800))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. NVIDIA Nsight Compute (`ncu`): Micro-Kernel Hardware Counters\n",
    "Profile the naive Mandelbrot kernel to observe **Warp Execution Efficiency** and **Speed-of-Light** metrics."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!ncu --section SpeedOfLight \\\n",
    "     --section WarpStateStats \\\n",
    "     --force-overwrite \\\n",
    "     --export telemetry/colab_ncu_mandelbrot \\\n",
    "     ./src/mandelbrot/mandelbrot_cuda 1024 1024 256 1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Compare with Nsight Compute Snapshot\n",
    "Observe the low Warp Execution Efficiency (< 20%) in naive fractal rendering due to SIMT divergence."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "display(Image(\"presentation/images/snapshots/snapshot_ncu_micro_dashboard.png\", width=800))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. PyTorch Profiler: Diagnosing the 86.2% D2H Host Stall\n",
    "Runs the PyTorch Mandelbrot suite and exports a Chrome/Perfetto JSON trace."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!python scripts/profile_torch.py"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Compare with PyTorch Profiler Snapshot"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "display(Image(\"presentation/images/snapshots/snapshot_torch_profiler_trace.png\", width=800))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Download Traces to Your Local Machine\n",
    "Download the generated `.nsys-rep` and `.ncu-rep` files to inspect them in the free local desktop GUIs (`nsys-ui` and `ncu-ui`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "# Download Nsight Systems report\n",
    "files.download('telemetry/colab_nsys_gemm.nsys-rep')\n",
    "# Download Nsight Compute report\n",
    "files.download('telemetry/colab_ncu_mandelbrot.ncu-rep')\n",
    "# Download PyTorch Perfetto trace\n",
    "files.download('telemetry/torch_trace_gemm.json')"
   ]
  }
